      "name": "User permission switches",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "Existing square Toggle reused for individual user permissions; three columns on wide screens, two on compact desktop and one on mobile. Static checked-state previews; the application supplies persistence and request disabling.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-permissions\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Permissions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ds-permission\" role=\"switch\" aria-checked=\"true\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\"><i></i></span>Start server</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ds-permission\" role=\"switch\" aria-checked=\"false\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\"><i></i></span>Read console</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ds-permission\" role=\"switch\" aria-checked=\"false\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\"><i></i></span>Manage users</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-permissions{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:4px;border-top:2px solid var(--red,#ff6477);padding-top:18px}.ds-permission{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;min-height:44px;padding:8px;border:0;border-radius:0;background:transparent;font:13px 'IBM Plex Sans',sans-serif;color:var(--muted,#c3abb2);text-align:left;cursor:pointer}.ds-permission>span{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:flex-end;flex-shrink:0;width:34px;height:18px;padding:3px;border:1px solid var(--cyan,#74e7e9)}.ds-permission i{display:block;width:10px;height:10px;background:var(--cyan,#74e7e9)}.ds-permission[aria-checked=false]>span{justify-content:flex-start;border-color:var(--line,#834653)}.ds-permission[aria-checked=false] i{background:var(--muted,#c3abb2)}.ds-permission:hover:not(:disabled){background:#3b202b}.ds-permission:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--cyan,#74e7e9);outline-offset:4px}.ds-permission:disabled{opacity:.45;cursor:not-allowed}@media(max-width:1100px){.ds-permissions{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}@media(max-width:720px){.ds-permissions{grid-template-columns:1fr}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Cyberpunk server operations",
    "overview": "The user-pinned direction is a Cyberpunk operating surface. Dark charcoal and plum panels carry sharp red contours, cyan operational information and selective yellow action accents. IBM Plex typography and generous separation keep the expressive palette readable during server administration.\n\nThis system replaces the former green, rounded interface. Preserve the approved dark, angular identity across Dashboard, Console, Bundles, Settings, Users, sign-in and first-run setup. English and German share the same visual hierarchy and control behavior; longer translations must wrap without obscuring an action or state.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Dark tonal surfaces and angular red contours.",
      "Cyan operational information and visible focus.",
      "Selective yellow actions and active selections.",
      "Readable English/German controls and native output interaction."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The State Text Rule",
        "body": "Colored square indicators always accompany readable status text. Cyan is positive operational information; disabled controls and stale or unknown bundle states must not imply confirmed availability.",
        "section": "colors"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do preserve the red/cyan/yellow roles and dark angular surfaces selected by the user.",
      "Do keep state text, visible labels, keyboard access and cyan focus outlines alongside visual indicators.",
      "Do preserve wrapping and responsive stacking for both English and German.",
      "Do keep Console selection/scrolling usable and require confirmed bundle control availability."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't restore the former green palette or rounded control language.",
      "Don't present unrelated settings feedback after navigation or infer stopped state from empty output.",
      "Don't treat synthetic review fixtures as product defaults or describe this bounded review as a complete accessibility or backend audit."
    ]
  }
}
